 "about": "InDesign 2025 (20.5.5.119) table size limits by DOM. create: Table.add with bodyRowCount/columnCount/headerRowCount/footerRowCount (each has its own range: body 1-10000, columns 1-200, header 0-25, footer 0-25; the sum is not limited: 9999 body + 1 header + 1 footer = 10001 rows is made). setup: the same fields as properties of an existing table (Table Options > Table Setup). grow: Rows.add, Columns.add and Cell.split have no limit of their own (a table reached 13000 rows by Rows.add, 251 columns by Columns.add, 10001 rows and 201 columns by split; \"Cells too small to split\" is a size message of a 9999-row table in a 500 pt frame, not a count). Probe: next/oracle/indesign/tablelimit-probe.jsx.",
